  "outdir": "exports",
  "previewdir": "previews",
  "_notes": [
    "Every single-pulley case is one connected body. 'Size set' is four, one",
    "per tooth count, and that count is itself the test -- an earlier build had",
    "all four slots reading the global tooth count and printing the same wheel.",
    "max_bbox doubles as the build-volume check: 256mm is a Bambu X1/P1 plate,",
    "tighter caps are set on the cases that once blew past them.",
    "euler is not asserted. A split clamp legitimately adds handles (bore, screw",
    "hole, and the loop the slot and screw make together), so the number tracks",
    "the clamp mode rather than defect-freedom, and bodies + watertight already",
    "carry the load.",
    "The 'rejected' cases are the guards. A generator that refuses a bad",
    "parameter set is only trustworthy if the refusal is tested too -- and the",
    "string match means the guard has to fail for the right reason, not just",
    "fail. Both were found by measurement, not by reading the code:",
    "  8T with the default 5mm bore exported 2 disconnected bodies;",
    "  flange_height 10 on a 6mm belt exported 21, and hung 1mm below the plate.",
    "teeth_150 carries a degenerate-face allowance. Extruding all 150 grooves as one drawing leaves a dozen zero-area slivers where neighbouring groove outlines meet -- the per-groove version left none, but took 394s instead of 50s. The slivers carry no area, the mesh stays watertight and single-bodied, and slicers drop them.",
    "",
    "The tooth ceiling is 75, and it is a render-time limit rather than a",
    "geometry one. Tooth count is the only parameter that meaningfully drives",
    "render cost: 150T measured 394s before the cutter rewrite and 50s after,",
    "75T measures 34s. Everything else -- belt width, hub length, flange size,",
    "bore -- changes extrude heights and a few cylinder diameters and does not",
    "move the number.",
    "",
    "The plate guard is measured, not estimated. Predicted width for the default",
    "set (16/20/30/40 GT2) is 88.46mm against an exported 88.5. It measures from",
    "the hub as well as the flange, because on a small wheel with a clamping hub",
    "the hub is the wider of the two, and the default set proves it: without the",
    "hub term the prediction is 86.25mm and 2.25mm short.",
    "",
    "out_size_set_4x75_gt2 carries a degenerate-face allowance, like teeth_max_75",
    "would have at 150. 300 groove outlines extruded as one drawing leave a few",
    "collinear slivers where neighbours meet: 18 of 148224 faces, area exactly",
    "0.0, cross product exactly 0.0, and the mesh is watertight, winding-",
    "consistent, four bodies, Euler -16 -- which is four genus-3 pulleys, exactly",
    "what four split-clamp wheels should be. Slicers drop them.",
    "",
    "That case is also the heaviest thing the sliders can reach: 98.6s and",
    "209.8mm wide against a predicted 209.75."
  ],
